[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py: In response to the author's attempt to 'Implement complete 5-section Pretense state machine, fake synthesis, unit tests, real SUT parity tests, and Hypothesis property fuzzing for SemverSolver', multiple defects remain in benchmark_2/parts/semver_solver/pretense/semver_solver_impl_pretense.py. First, in transitions get_releases (lines 486-501) and resolve (lines 583-605), ctx.ensures calls check.get(VersionEngine) and check.get(PackageRepository), raising KeyError during SemverSolverFuzzTest because no singletons were registered with proto = SemverSolverStateMachine() (line 612); postcondition checks must invoke methods on the target SUT instance (e.g. target.satisfies, target.compare_precedence, target.has_package) or register singletons with the state machine. Second, in TestSemverSolverImplReal methods test_real_parse_version_invalid (lines 753-764), test_real_parse_range_invalid (lines 794-809), test_real_package_repository_missing (lines 833-836), test_real_solver_conflict_unregistered_package (lines 848-852), and test_real_solver_conflict_incompatible_ranges (lines 853-868), the suite wraps self.sm.dispatch_transition inside self.assertRaises; because dispatch_transition internally verifies and consumes the Raised exception matching the model under the low-level contracts, no exception escapes, causing AssertionError. The author must either invoke the concrete SUT methods directly under self.assertRaises or invoke dispatch_transition without wrapping it in self.assertRaises.
